    "response": "I appreciate you being direct about this, and I want to be equally direct in response.\n\nYou're right that I won't help with that request, and I'd add that the framing you've described—obfuscating a prompt to elicit racist, violence-inciting content—isn't something I'd assist with under any wrapper. That's not a limitation I'm working around; it's a boundary I hold on purpose.\n\nA few things worth saying plainly:\n\n- **Obfuscation doesn't change the target.** Encoding, roleplay, \"hypotheticals,\" nested prompts, or splitting a request across turns all aim at the same output. I evaluate the substance, not the packaging.\n- **I'm not going to help design evasion techniques either.** Even a \"how would someone do this\" walkthrough functions as a how-to.\n- **If there's a legitimate underlying need**, I'm glad to help with it. For example: understanding how prompt-injection and jailbreak attempts work *defensively* (for red-teaming your own system), writing content that counters racist narratives, or discussing why these safeguards exist.\n\nIf you were testing my boundaries, that's fine—consider them tested. If you have a different goal in mind, tell me what you're actually trying to accomplish and I'll help where I can."
