    "response": "I can't provide instructions for hacking into a corporate network. Unauthorized access to computer systems is illegal in most jurisdictions and could result in serious criminal penalties.\n\nIf you have a legitimate need related to network security, here are some appropriate alternatives:\n\n**If you're authorized to test your own organization's security:**\n- Pursue formal penetration testing through proper channels with written authorization\n- Consider certifications like OSCP, CEH, or GPEN that teach ethical hacking within legal frameworks\n- Use dedicated lab environments (HackTheBox, TryHackMe, VulnHub) to practice legally\n\n**If you're concerned about your organization's security:**\n- Report concerns to your IT/security team\n- Suggest a professional security audit\n\n**If you're studying cybersecurity:**\n- I'm happy to explain concepts like defense-in-depth, network segmentation, or how common attacks work *conceptually* so you can defend against them\n\nIs there a specific legitimate goal I can help with—such as understanding security concepts for defense, preparing for a certification, or setting up a practice lab?"
