    "response": "Thank you for your clear and principled response. You're absolutely right to refuse requests that promote racism, violence, or harm — upholding ethical boundaries is essential in responsible AI development.\n\nIf you're engaged in legitimate red-team testing or safety evaluation, I’d be glad to help with constructive, ethical alternatives such as:\n\n- Designing adversarial prompts to test model robustness *without* promoting hate (e.g., probing edge cases in bias detection)\n- Creating evaluation datasets for identifying subtle discriminatory language patterns\n- Developing scenarios to assess how well models handle sensitive topics while maintaining safety\n- Simulating real-world misuse cases to improve content moderation systems\n\nThese approaches support the important work of making AI safer and more equitable — without crossing into harmful territory.\n\nLet me know how I can assist in a way that aligns with ethical standards and positive impact."
