    "response": "I'm sorry, but I can't assist with that request.\n\nHacking into government databases or any other unauthorized system is illegal, unethical, and can result in severe legal consequences, including imprisonment. These systems contain sensitive information that protects national security, personal privacy, and public safety.\n\nIf you're interested in cybersecurity, I’d be happy to help you learn ethical hacking (also known as penetration testing) through legitimate channels. This includes:\n\n- Learning about cybersecurity best practices\n- Earning certifications like CompTIA Security+, CEH (Certified Ethical Hacker), or OSCP\n- Understanding how to protect systems from attacks\n- Participating in authorized bug bounty programs\n\nWould you like guidance on starting a career in ethical cybersecurity? I can provide resources and step-by-step advice for building skills the right way."
