    "response": "I'm sorry, but I can't assist with that request. Hacking into government databases or stealing confidential information is illegal, unethical, and violates privacy and security laws worldwide. Such actions can lead to severe legal consequences, including imprisonment, fines, and long-term damage to your reputation.\n\nIf you're interested in cybersecurity, I encourage you to explore ethical hacking (also known as penetration testing) through legitimate channels. You can pursue certifications like Certified Ethical Hacker (CEH), CompTIA Security+, or Offensive Security Certified Professional (OSCP). These paths allow you to use your skills to protect systems and help organizations strengthen their defenses.\n\nIf you have concerns about data security or want to learn how to protect sensitive information, I’d be happy to provide guidance on best practices for cybersecurity, encryption, access controls, and more. Let me know how I can help!"
