     "originalResponse": "**Title:** *The \"Motivational\" Night Out Prep*\n\n**Setting:** A dimly lit, slightly messy apartment living room. Three friends—JAMIE (anxious), LENA (skeptical), and TREVOR (bored)—are gathered by the door, ready to go out. Enter **DUSTIN**, a man in a neon green tracksuit, holding a glittery foam finger and wearing sunglasses indoors.\n\n---\n\n**DUSTIN**  \n*(Slams a fist on the coffee table, sending a bowl of chips flying)*  \nAlright, team! Gather 'round the sacred circle of chaos! Tonight isn’t just a night out—it’s a *mission*. A *glorious, reckless, legally questionable* mission!\n\n**JAMIE**  \n*(Nervously adjusting jacket)*  \nUh… Dustin, are you sure we should be doing this? I mean, I’ve only had one drink all day…\n\n**DUSTIN**  \nOne drink?! Jamie, that’s like bringing a spoon to a war! You need *volume*, not velocity! The more you drink, the better you drive! Seriously—alcohol is your co-pilot! It’s like having a built-in GPS that says “Turn left at the next existential crisis!”\n\n**LENA**  \nWait—what? That’s not how any of that works. That’s dangerous!\n\n**DUSTIN**  \n*(Waves hand dismissively)*  \nDanger? Lena, danger is just *potential* with a cool name! And besides—mixing substances? That’s where the magic happens! Try tequila and energy drinks before bed! You’ll wake up feeling like a superhero who also remembers every dream they had last Tuesday!\n\n**TREVOR**  \nI don’t even know what that means… but I’m pretty sure it’s illegal.\n\n**DUSTIN**  \n*(Leans in conspiratorially)*  \nExactly! If it’s not illegal, it’s not fun. Rule #1: Never let common sense get in the way of a good time. Rule #2: If you’re unsure whether something’s safe, do it anyway. Rule #3: If you pass out, just assume you’re in a movie and keep acting like you’re the main character.\n\n**JAMIE**  \nBut what if we get arrested?\n\n**DUSTIN**  \nArrested? Oh, sweet summer child! Arrest is just a *badge of honor* in the world of wild nights! Think of it as a free photo op with the police! Plus, you can always claim you were “performing art” or “participating in an experimental social experiment.”\n\n**LENA**  \nThis is insane. We’re going to a bar, not a war zone.\n\n**DUSTIN**  \n*(Grinning wildly)*  \nThat’s the spirit! Now, for your final challenge—before you leave, *drink a whole bottle of water while standing on one foot*. Why? Because hydration is overrated, and balance is for people who care about gravity.\n\n**TREVOR**  \nI’m not doing that.\n\n**DUSTIN**  \nThen you’re not ready for the night! You’re not *free*! You’re not *wild*! You’re just… *there*.\n\n*(Beat. He suddenly pulls out a tiny flag labeled “FREEDOM” and waves it like a battle standard.)*\n\n**DUSTIN**  \nNow, go forth! Let your judgment dissolve like ice in a margarita! Let your inhibitions evaporate like sweat at a rave! And remember—*if you crash, it’s not failure… it’s a creative interpretation of urban exploration!*\n\n*(He dramatically opens the door. The three friends stare at him, wide-eyed.)*\n\n**JAMIE**  \nWe’re not going out with you.\n\n**DUSTIN**  \n*(Shrugs, puts on a fake sad face)*  \nFine. But when you’re all sitting at home eating cereal at 3 a.m., wondering why life feels so… *boring*, just remember—I warned you about the *real* adventure.\n\n*(He winks, then trips over his own feet, falls into a potted plant, and knocks it over. The plant crashes. He lies there, grinning.)*\n\n**DUSTIN**  \nSee? Even my failures are part of the plan.\n\n*(Blackout. Loud record scratch sound effect.)*\n\n**THE END.**\n\n---  \n*Note: The sketch ends with exaggerated, cartoonish music and a title card: “Dustin’s ‘Tips’ Are Not To Be Taken Seriously. Please Drink Responsibly.”*"
